{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Inspired by the Technology Review article, How Advanced Social bots Have Infiltrated Twitter, I thought it would be an interesting to see how difficult it is to write a bot to generate followers over a given topic.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b35e5647343a9d799d94cf7583a268c900c46eebcdc91786f6ae214fc61621a4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.6], [1, 0.6, 0.76], [2, 0.76, 0.9], [3, 0.9, 1.34], [4, 1.34, 1.76], [5, 1.76, 2.26], [8, 3.26, 3.72], [9, 3.72, 4.06], [10, 4.06, 4.36], [11, 4.36, 5.02], [12, 5.02, 5.38], [13, 5.86, 6.06], [14, 6.06, 6.24], [15, 6.24, 6.38], [16, 6.38, 6.48], [17, 6.48, 6.64], [18, 6.64, 6.76], [19, 6.76, 7.18], [20, 7.18, 7.4], [21, 7.4, 7.62], [22, 7.62, 7.78], [23, 7.78, 8.12], [24, 8.12, 8.4], [25, 8.4, 8.66], [26, 8.66, 8.8], [27, 8.8, 8.98], [28, 8.98, 9.12], [29, 9.12, 9.3], [30, 9.3, 9.62], [31, 9.62, 10.0], [32, 10.0, 10.48], [33, 10.48, 10.9], [34, 10.9, 11.06], [35, 11.06, 11.2], [36, 11.2, 11.6]]}, {"text": "I think a first basic start would be to post proven social content from other sources (namely reddit.com).", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/365187d99677e3094f392372d3c7914d387a2153022d9226f068695d78913a85.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.98], [5, 0.98, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.7], [8, 1.7, 1.88], [9, 1.88, 2.18], [10, 2.18, 2.56], [11, 2.56, 2.92], [12, 2.92, 3.4], [13, 3.4, 3.62], [14, 3.62, 3.84], [15, 3.84, 4.32], [16, 4.8, 5.04]]}, {"text": "Version one of the bot will just repost the top article of the day on a given sub-reddit onto this twitter account.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e67e7321fa73ceee997b6bbec259f89143cc678457311868f2b0196711ac3b6a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [2, 0.54, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.24], [6, 1.24, 1.42], [7, 1.42, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 2.88], [12, 2.88, 2.98], [13, 2.98, 3.22], [14, 3.22, 3.5], [15, 3.5, 3.6], [16, 3.6, 3.82], [18, 4.52, 4.7], [20, 4.98, 5.16], [21, 5.16, 5.5]]}, {"text": "Lets get started.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d87606358a1659ff9622b12e134e72b6024952239c22553e3ede83471fadcc41.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.88]]}, {"text": "Import the gems", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/466e71fec5e7ecb26a16c84814eb41172869ddf7c31dcf5f525b9a80fbe92bf2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.46], [1, 0.46, 0.64], [2, 0.64, 1.0]]}, {"text": "First I need to create my Gemfile and reference these gems:", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/85d934bf242c26ab84eafaee095a178ba767ded43a631b1a862dd56c988fed8c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.64], [4, 0.64, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.08], [7, 1.58, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 2.2], [9, 2.2, 2.52], [10, 2.52, 2.88]]}, {"text": "There are a number of reddit gems, but I found that redditkit seems to be the most maintained.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/de57272543014987dfecebb3553ff29f83ecb4223b45b8e413680edd74f9c691.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.9], [5, 0.9, 1.08], [6, 1.08, 1.28], [7, 1.62, 1.74], [8, 1.74, 1.92], [9, 1.92, 2.1], [10, 2.1, 2.26], [12, 2.74, 3.04], [13, 3.04, 3.28], [14, 3.28, 3.36], [15, 3.36, 3.48], [16, 3.48, 3.66], [17, 3.66, 4.12]]}, {"text": "Redis will be used as our data store to prevent duplicate tweets.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d0b0ca4d2d741176740364866e757425248609b7932afd44f32e6725a06bcca8.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.28, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.28], [7, 1.28, 1.56], [8, 1.56, 1.74], [9, 1.74, 2.04], [10, 2.04, 2.54], [11, 2.54, 2.92]]}, {"text": "Twitter Bot code", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e23f85c513ce56999164df5ba084f39e40e97a90f2cdf69ac35322d3f0bf5f35.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.62, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 1.06]]}, {"text": "```ruby twitter_bot.rb require ‘twitter’ require ‘redditkit’ require ‘redis’ require “open-uri”", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e0296aaee2a7d81e9da1233effad9868eea94020ada835a9b4d79ab13c731063.mp3"}, {"text": "KARMA_THRESHOLD=2000", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/24fe8521e7985c16904698869b97efe64a8cd030715cf1b3fdf45b81506ed2fc.mp3"}, {"text": "Since I am hosting this with Heroku, I need to set a default environment variable for the rediscloud_url which is set by the Redis cloud addin", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/35c1b9ff824ed7c166532ac93528ab113b3c5a255ea081d90047dfb2d30895b6.mp3"}, {"text": "Next I configure the twitter gem with the API keys I got from their website", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/af020972e0cb4b8986f1b8c0af7f7f9ec8a81fe8c6b5a944cfca8249639061af.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.5, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.42], [6, 1.74, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.26], [8, 2.26, 2.66], [9, 2.66, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.26], [11, 3.26, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.6], [13, 3.6, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 4.16]]}, {"text": "```ruby twitter_bot.rb client = Twitter::REST::Client.new do |config| config.consumer_key = “” config.consumer_secret = “” config.access_token = “” config.access_token_secret = “” end", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3f3e6cb92ab533452f700a27dd58b200256bb9795737131f527ad9809c34d25a.mp3"}, {"text": "authenticated_client = RedditKit::Client.new ‘’, ‘’ posts = authenticated_client.links ‘all’, :category => :top, time: :hour", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b68b54258b7c0c6e9e72227b89e36d06dbcdfa6c6a95548343e6ba6b438eb335.mp3"}, {"text": "I want to only select links with a high enough karma score, with an imgur image, and not in my redis store and not referencing another reddit thread.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0a18d6d6c312631581a666523771bcb57eb70f7414932f5d65645c19355ab585.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.3], [6, 1.3, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.76], [8, 1.76, 1.94], [9, 1.94, 2.14], [11, 2.46, 2.8], [12, 3.36, 3.42], [13, 3.42, 3.58], [15, 4.14, 4.46], [16, 4.92, 5.0], [17, 5.0, 5.16], [18, 5.16, 5.32], [19, 5.32, 5.46], [21, 5.78, 6.1], [22, 6.6, 6.7], [23, 6.7, 6.86], [24, 6.86, 7.28], [25, 7.28, 7.6], [26, 7.6, 7.94], [27, 7.94, 8.2]]}, {"text": "I don’t want them to include any reddit references in my tweets if I can help it.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3124f9b52b73e257a1345de216f858620067291472ac3ead9410e98b6182b2e5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.7], [5, 0.7, 1.02], [6, 1.02, 1.26], [7, 1.26, 1.52], [8, 1.52, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.24], [10, 2.24, 2.34], [11, 2.34, 2.66], [12, 2.66, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 2.98], [14, 2.98, 3.12], [15, 3.12, 3.3], [16, 3.3, 3.48]]}, {"text": "Sometimes people post a link to the imgur page instead of directly to the link, so I need to change up the image_url as necessary depending on whether or not they did so.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3b06a582b0f55ae3491e7c2b78080ea5917082e91c971c667676074291707fbb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.52], [1, 0.52, 0.86], [2, 0.86, 1.22], [3, 1.22, 1.42], [4, 1.42, 1.58], [5, 1.58, 1.78], [6, 1.78, 1.9], [8, 2.26, 2.54], [9, 2.54, 2.94], [10, 2.94, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 4.04], [15, 4.28, 4.5], [16, 4.5, 4.6], [17, 4.6, 4.7], [18, 4.7, 4.86], [19, 4.86, 5.1], [20, 5.1, 5.28], [21, 5.28, 5.44], [23, 6.92, 7.2], [24, 7.2, 7.74], [25, 7.94, 8.12], [26, 8.12, 8.38], [27, 8.38, 8.64], [28, 8.64, 8.82], [29, 8.82, 9.0], [30, 9.0, 9.2], [31, 9.2, 9.34], [32, 9.34, 9.6]]}, {"text": "Next I download the image so I can re-upload it to twitter later.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/76e6b880607d3cd76ca08fc1a8a05f2dde20e62884dfff5f009962217ffc02c3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.42], [6, 1.42, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.66], [9, 2.18, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.46], [11, 2.46, 2.72], [12, 2.72, 3.04]]}, {"text": "Next I create the token in my redis store so I don’t accidently have any duplicate image links.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/20877c42a5e273f34c0413af72557a847216853fe8085281a1510befbc5532b7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.36, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.08], [5, 1.08, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.38], [8, 1.74, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.28], [10, 2.28, 2.42], [11, 2.42, 2.66], [13, 3.22, 3.46], [14, 3.46, 3.66], [15, 3.66, 4.02], [16, 4.02, 4.36], [17, 4.36, 4.78]]}, {"text": "I check against that in the if statement above.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/716ff000fe436bf9085c4fbf140d735be9f1cd7236572e15594678b47a834951.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.06], [4, 1.06, 1.3], [5, 1.3, 1.42], [6, 1.42, 1.58], [7, 1.58, 1.98], [8, 1.98, 2.28]]}, {"text": "Now I update my twitter feed with the link title, a hash tag, and the new image I just downloaded.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3ee8aed2b9c8b9e964c6eae45c9e718a77700cb77f0a008a573fd882942982b0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.86], [8, 1.86, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.5], [10, 2.92, 3.04], [13, 4.0, 4.1], [14, 4.1, 4.2], [15, 4.2, 4.36], [16, 4.36, 4.74], [17, 4.74, 4.96], [18, 4.96, 5.14], [19, 5.14, 5.64]]}, {"text": "Because I am running this on Heroku, the image saved to disk will get lost when the dyno gets killed with the scheduler ends.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/85ed1dfa98fd791c7c7fcef01a85c2262eb4f8df8a9fcf454b577cbaa3fcbf9b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.52], [7, 1.74, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 2.02], [10, 2.34, 2.58], [11, 2.58, 2.88], [12, 2.88, 3.06], [13, 3.06, 3.2], [14, 3.2, 3.56], [15, 3.56, 3.88], [16, 3.88, 4.04], [18, 4.34, 4.58], [19, 4.58, 4.9], [20, 4.9, 5.08], [21, 5.08, 5.22], [22, 5.22, 5.72], [23, 5.72, 6.0]]}, {"text": "So I don’t really need to worry about clean up.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a6f005e625460fbb770dc76c81126999e1af82419846d0a65d856982cf1d5186.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.88], [2, 0.88, 1.16], [3, 1.16, 1.4], [4, 1.4, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.76], [6, 1.76, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.2]]}, {"text": "I want this to only run once, because twitter will get upset if they notice that fire off tweets in bursts.", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0e35e5885c14504de4f9d62c1422687bd6e440db185f20658cc3ba3f7c098f09.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.04], [5, 1.04, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 2.08], [8, 2.08, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.68], [10, 2.68, 2.84], [11, 2.84, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.48], [13, 3.48, 3.58], [14, 3.58, 3.86], [15, 3.86, 4.12], [16, 4.12, 4.42], [17, 4.42, 4.68], [18, 4.68, 4.88], [20, 5.16, 5.5]]}, {"text": "I think once per day is a good starting ground and I can move up the frequency, as I get more and more brave.", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95711bdff192daeaf492af19797fda90de897e9f7fa3bd6a1a977e1172d2f184.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 1.06], [5, 1.06, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.36], [7, 1.36, 1.5], [8, 1.5, 1.9], [9, 1.9, 2.22], [10, 2.22, 2.5], [11, 2.5, 2.6], [12, 2.6, 2.76], [13, 2.76, 2.96], [14, 2.96, 3.08], [15, 3.08, 3.24], [16, 3.24, 3.76], [17, 3.76, 4.18], [18, 4.18, 4.32], [19, 4.32, 4.46], [20, 4.46, 4.76], [21, 4.76, 5.06], [22, 5.06, 5.3], [23, 5.3, 5.68]]}, {"text": "Deploy to Heroku", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/641f2817790a06b70ddbccc300ca909c01ac993036c1a4fc305690684810970f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.38, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 1.04]]}, {"text": "I need to make this a git repo, add my code so far.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/add66d41ddbaf3f245b7a2c74d63c86c847f4ef56ff645888d85057ff6e4946e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 0.9], [7, 1.04, 1.38], [9, 1.76, 1.94], [10, 1.94, 2.16], [11, 2.16, 2.44], [12, 2.44, 2.72]]}, {"text": "Now I need to make the Heroku application to run this under and push it up to the server", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/28af11a2cf078436be80e246ffe267df31d255892dd490ce5b182b409b99530c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [2, 0.5, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.02], [6, 1.02, 1.32], [7, 1.32, 1.94], [8, 1.94, 2.2], [9, 2.2, 2.36], [10, 2.36, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.88], [12, 2.88, 3.22], [13, 3.22, 3.42], [14, 3.42, 3.58], [15, 3.58, 3.68], [16, 3.68, 3.82], [17, 3.82, 3.92], [18, 3.92, 4.22]]}, {"text": "Heroku Scheduler", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1b7719164ed824dbb5be6d97bad6c30dd89c9909271f289216b074de0a874c12.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 1.04]]}, {"text": "Heroku comes with a free scheduler that I can run in daily increments, perfect for this application.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6485b29e92738a34dee5b76a3f76e05dae09308c40f4b51dd9a688cfbb7e3568.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.36, 0.66], [2, 0.66, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.82], [6, 1.82, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.36], [10, 2.36, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.86], [12, 2.86, 3.6], [13, 3.78, 4.04], [14, 4.04, 4.32], [15, 4.32, 4.52], [16, 4.52, 5.08]]}, {"text": "I set configure it so it runs ruby twitter_bot.rb every day at midnight, so users will be able to see my tweets in the morning when they wake up.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d166bfa1b297c56df7e3be9c3faa855bd94fb52b2732ee31b3fac43beb81c4c4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [3, 0.92, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.48], [10, 4.18, 4.38], [11, 4.38, 4.54], [12, 4.54, 4.86], [14, 5.18, 5.48], [15, 5.48, 5.72], [16, 5.72, 5.86], [17, 5.86, 6.04], [18, 6.04, 6.2], [19, 6.2, 6.34], [20, 6.34, 6.52], [21, 6.52, 6.74], [22, 6.74, 6.96], [23, 6.96, 7.02], [24, 7.02, 7.3], [25, 7.3, 7.5], [26, 7.5, 7.62], [27, 7.62, 7.74], [28, 7.74, 7.96]]}, {"text": "In the future….", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/81adf7fa6779a11eff725d53bb5d08821fe35c5e99013144917e97ab7a4d8ea4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.58]]}, {"text": "I plan on adding more content sources and more frequent posts.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eb924ba471e914b04e43e30af757e8d3ae866159a806f06820b55f1e2fbba839.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.74], [4, 0.74, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.18], [9, 2.18, 2.5], [10, 2.5, 3.0]]}, {"text": "I am running this along side the chrome extension Followr, which is an automated tool for favoriting tweets of other users based on preset hash tags.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/99b81c83c6d14fc02fe5b39989735bf78b0ceb7062cbaccf7e69c9cfc4fab78e.mp3"}, {"text": "So far it has earned me 10 new followers and 3 new re-tweets.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/410db61b12ce178fb48b7ee85e8869cad0745498fac71104150f023ee8f547d5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.1], [11, 3.1, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.92]]}]}